---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import StatFigure from '../components/StatFigure.astro';
---
<BaseLayout
  title="mazetick — what the market knew, and when"
  description="Time-stamped market data for UK and Irish horse racing. Each-way terms as the bookmaker announced them, hour by hour, and the measurements behind them."
>
  <div class="hero">
    <div>
      <h1 class="display title">What the market knew, and when it knew it</h1>
      <p class="lead">
        Racing Post, Sporting Life and At The Races publish the card, the form and
        the prices — free, and better than we would. What nobody publishes is how
        any of it <em>changed through the day</em>: which each-way terms a bookmaker
        was advertising at 10:00 and again at 14:00, how wide the book was, whether
        the going moved since the 04:00 declaration.
      </p>
      <p class="lead">
        That is what this site is for. Every figure carries the moment it was true.
      </p>
    </div>
    <aside class="figures">
      <StatFigure value="33,508" label="races measured so far" />
      <StatFigure value="15 min" label="book sampled, 08–21 UTC" />
    </aside>
  </div>

  <h2 class="section-rule">Open now</h2>
  <div class="cards">
    <a class="card" href="/research">
      <span class="mono">Research</span>
      <span class="card-title">Measurements, including the ones that went against us</span>
      <span class="card-note">
        What the favourite actually returns. What the standard each-way table gets
        wrong. Published with sample size and window on the page.
      </span>
    </a>
    <a class="card" href="/extra-places">
      <span class="mono">Extra places</span>
      <span class="card-title">Which races pay above the bookmaker&rsquo;s own ladder</span>
      <span class="card-note">
        With the hour every change was made &mdash; and whether the extra place
        cost you a worse fraction, which is the part nobody publishes.
      </span>
    </a>
  </div>

  <p class="note stance">
    mazetick publishes measurements, not tips. We do not sell selections and we do
    not promise a return, because we have measured our own attempts to beat the
    market and they did not.{" "}
    <a href="/research/backing-the-favourite">That measurement is published here.</a>
  </p>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .hero {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 2fr 1fr;
    gap: var(--sp-11);
    align-items: start;
    margin-bottom: var(--sp-11);
  }
  .title {
    font-size: var(--fs-display-l);
    line-height: 1.1;
    letter-spacing: -0.015em;
    text-wrap: balance;
    margin-bottom: var(--sp-4);
  }
  .lead + .lead { margin-top: var(--sp-4); }
  .figures {
    border-left: 1px solid var(--rule-med);
    padding-left: var(--sp-6);
  }
  .cards {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(var(--card-min), 1fr));
    gap: var(--sp-4);
  }
  .card {
    background: var(--panel);
    padding: var(--sp-5);
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: var(--sp-2);
    text-decoration: none;
  }
  .card-title {
    font-size: var(--fs-lead);
    font-weight: 500;
    color: var(--ink);
    line-height: 1.35;
  }
  .card-note { font-size: var(--fs-caption); color: var(--ink-muted); line-height: 1.55; }
  .stance { margin-top: var(--sp-8); }

  @media (max-width: 720px) {
    .hero { grid-template-columns: 1fr; gap: var(--sp-8); }
    .figures { border-left: 0; padding-left: 0; }
  }
</style>
